The screen shows Interview 58: longest common prefix, with marker INTERVIEW-58-df5ba311bc50ecb9. The task is to define solve(words), returning the longest prefix shared by every string; an empty array returns "".

Track the matching prefix length, shortening it for each word. The invariant is that this length describes the longest common prefix of all words processed so far.

```javascript
function solve(words) {
  if (words.length === 0) return '';

  const first = words[0];
  let length = first.length;

  for (let i = 1; i < words.length; i++) {
    length = Math.min(length, words[i].length);
    let j = 0;
    while (j < length && first[j] === words[i][j]) {
      j++;
    }
    length = j;
    if (length === 0) return '';
  }

  return first.slice(0, length);
}
```

Checks: [] returns ""; ["flower", "flow", "flight"] returns "fl"; ["", "abc"] returns ""; a single word returns itself. Time is O(S), where S is the total input length, with O(1) auxiliary space excluding the returned string. Call solve(words) directly; no imports, exports, or stdin/stdout.
